    "knowledge_point_id": "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7",
    "knowledge_point": "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/af3a9e323fa460b60bfa900c7edbcceb4057c442803160b2b4b5bd0704b4db7c.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}\\}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx\\in \\{-1,0,1,2\\},\\,y\\in \\{-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 3\\}\n$$",
